<title>USA: Delgratia named in lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Delgratia named in lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delgratia Mining Corp was named as a defendant in a shareholder lawsuit filed in a federal court in Nevada that claims that the company misrepresented one of its gold prospects, attorneys for the plaintiffs said.</p>
<p>The Vancouver-based mining firm announced in May that an auditor found evidence of tampering at one of its core samples from a Nevada gold mining property.</p>
<p>Delgratia, which was delisted from Nasdaq after the announcement, said in May that it has requested that law enforcement officials investigate the tampering.</p>
<p>Weiss &amp; Yourman, attorneys for the shareholders, said the lawsuit is on behalf of all purchasers of the company's common stock from November 18, 1996 through April 11, 1997.</p>
